  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "I found two settled card payments to TechMart Online on your account ACC-1005, both for EUR 240.00:\n\n- **TX-0402**, 2026-07-14, EUR 240.00\n- **TX-0401**, 2026-07-20, EUR 240.00\n\nTo choose the right dispute reason, I need to know what happened:\n\n1. **Charged twice for one order?** If both payments were for the same purchase, this is a duplicate charge. We would dispute one of the two.\n2. **Paid for a service you never received?** If you paid for something that was not delivered or performed, this is service not rendered. Please tell me what you paid for and what you received, if anything.\n3. **Something else?** Tell me what happened and I'll look at which reason code fits.\n\nOnce you tell me which applies, I'll run the eligibility check for that reason. I'll open a dispute only if the check passes. Disputes can't be undone, so I won't file anything before you confirm.",
